#
# A clause that passes today and is documented not to. One rule, not two: the branch that added this
# fixture warned about an empty-collection comparison as well, and this branch is the release that
# changes it -- `Sizes == 50` against `Sizes: []` now reports a failure, so the notice that warned
# about it was deleted along with the behaviour it described. A deprecation notice outliving its own
# change is how a warning becomes noise.
#
# `Name` is a string and the list holds integers, so nothing in the list can be compared with it.
# `NOT IN` reads that as "not a member" and passes, while `!=` on the same operands fails closed. That
# is unchanged here, so the notice stays.
#
rule incomparable_membership {
    Name not IN [10, 50, 100]
}
